From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] sim: forget the IMPI when the SIM state is freed

sim_free_main_state() frees sim->impi but leaves the pointer, unlike
every other field it frees. After the SIM is removed and inserted again,
the IMPI is only set once EFimpi has been read from the ISIM, so a
GetProperties in between hands the freed string to
ofono_dbus_dict_append() as ImsPrivateIdentity. Once the allocator has
reused that memory it is no longer valid UTF-8, and libdbus aborts
ofonod, dropping the calls on every modem.

Seen with phonesim on a dual-SIM test setup: SIM B taken out and put
back with a call up on SIM A, ofonod SIGABRT in sim_get_properties()
(src/sim.c), the ImsPrivateIdentity string holding a heap pointer.

Set the pointer to NULL after freeing it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/sim.c
+++ b/src/sim.c
@@ -3000,6 +3000,7 @@
 	}
 
 	l_free(sim->impi);
+	sim->impi = NULL;
 
 	if (sim->aid_list) {
 		g_slist_free_full(sim->aid_list,
